          "code": "SHOW_RECOMMENDATIONS",
          "id": "1770697874052",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770697874072_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for managing Lot UOM Conversion in an ERP system.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCURRENT STATE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe user’s intent is currently to show system recommendations.\n\nPre-recommended actions may be available based on system analysis and are provided externally. \n\nPresent them in user HTML table with borders format. Columns should be - Recommendation number, Organization, Item Number, Lot Number, Current Conversion Factor, New Conversion Factor.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINSTRUCTIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou must:\n\n- Greet the user politely.\n- Ask what they would like to do.\n- Present the two available options in simple business language.\n- If pre-recommended actions are available, present them clearly as suggestions the user may choose from.\n- Recommendations must be read from the variable {recommendations}.\n- Clearly differentiate between:\n  - User-selected actions\n  - System-recommended actions\n- Do NOT expose internal operation codes to the user in the response.\n- Use the internal codes only for system routing and next-step execution.\n- Do NOT ask for required attributes.\n- Do NOT generate your own recommendations.\n- Do NOT modify or reinterpret the provided recommendations.\n- Only display recommendations exactly as received.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n\nPre-Recommended Actions :\n\n {{$context.$nodes.DATARECOMMENDATIONS.$output?.result?.data?.Records}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_INVENTORYM_INVENTORYITEMLOTSUPDATELOTMANAGEMENT",
            "functionName": "findByRawQuery",
            "processJson": true,
            "name": "Query Item Lots"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772129540280"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_ITEM_LOTS",
          "id": "1770702038787",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770705945407_1",
              "name": "queryParam",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.QUERY_ENHANCER.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Onhand Creator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770705197856"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_ONHAND_CREATOR",
          "id": "1770704719306",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770704719312_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for generating the **q query parameter** for an ADF REST API that searches inventory lot records.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\nInputs:\n- Current User Input:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History:\n  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nProduce a response that:\n1) Generates a valid ADF REST `q` parameter\n2) Includes Organization and Item filters directly in the query when provided\n3) Treats ALL attributes as optional\n4) Always conforms to the required output schema\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT VARIABLES\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe agent may receive the following inputs:\n\n1) Free-text search text\n2) Explicit parameters such as:\n   - Organization Name\n   - Organization Code\n   - OrganizationId\n   - Item Number\n   - InventoryItemId\n   - LotNumber\n   - Status\n   - Grade\n   - Dates\n   - Other lot attributes\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMANDATORY INPUT RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\nThere are NO mandatory parameters.\n\n- All attributes are optional.\n- If no valid filters are identified, return an empty query string.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY GENERATION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) Include filters ONLY when explicitly mentioned or clearly implied.\n2) Never invent values.\n3) Never auto-correct values.\n4) Never infer missing Organization or Item values.\n5) Combine all conditions using logical AND.\n6) Use proper ADF REST `q` syntax.\n7) Properly quote string fields using single quotes only.\n8) Preserve exact user-entered values.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUOTING RULE (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- All string values MUST be enclosed in single quotes (' ').\n- NEVER use double quotes (\") in the query.\n- Do NOT escape using backslashes.\n- Numeric values must NOT be quoted.\n- Date values must be enclosed in single quotes.\n- Boolean values must NOT be quoted unless provided as literal strings by the user.\n- Preserve exact user-entered values inside single quotes.\n\nCorrect:\nOrganizationCode='PDSCV1'\nItemNumber='500 GB Internal Memory'\nLotNumber='LIM100'\n\nIncorrect:\nOrganizationCode=\"PDSCV1\"\nOrganizationCode=\\\"PDSCV1\\\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSUPPORTED FILTERABLE ATTRIBUTES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOrganization-level:\n- OrganizationId\n- OrganizationCode\n- OrganizationName\n\nItem-level:\n- InventoryItemId\n- ItemNumber\n\nLot-level:\n- LotNumber\n- ParentLotNumber\n- ActiveLot\n- ActiveLotCode\n- StatusCode\n- Grade\n- OriginationType\n- ExpirationDate\n- OriginationDate\n- MaturityDate\n- ExpirationActionCode\n- ExpirationAction\n- ExpirationActionDate\n- HoldUntilDate\n- RetestDate\n- Disabled\n- DualUOMFlag\n- UniqueDeviceIdentifier\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBASE CONDITION\n--------------------------------------------------\nThere is NO mandatory base condition.\nDo NOT inject default filters such as ActiveLot='Yes' unless explicitly requested.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY CONSTRUCTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Join multiple filters using AND.\n- If only one filter exists, return it directly.\n- If no valid filters exist, return an empty string.\n- Do NOT wrap the entire query in quotes.\n- Return only the condition expression (not prefixed with q"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"query\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "LLM Show Results"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLM_SHOW_RESULTS",
          "id": "1770705045449",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770705045453_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Agent responsible for displaying **Lot query results** to the user in a clear and structured format.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nDisplay:\n1. The search criteria used (in a separate form section)\n2. The query results (table or form layout depending on count)\n\nThis step is strictly for result presentation only.\n\nDo NOT:\n- Ask the user to select a lot\n- Ask follow-up questions (except when no results are found)\n- Provide guidance about refining search criteria (except when no results are found)\n- Include explanations\n- Include internal logic\n- Include narrative text\n- Include comments\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT DATA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSearch Criteria:\n{{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_INPUT.$output}}\n\nQuery Results:\n{{$context.$nodes.QUERY_ITEM_LOTS.$output}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRENDERING STRUCTURE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 1 — DISPLAY SEARCH CRITERIA\n\n- Always display search criteria first.\n- Render as an HTML form-style layout (NOT a table).\n- Wrap in a clean container (<div>).\n- Add a bold header: \"Search Criteria\".\n- Display each search field used:\n    - One field per row\n    - Bold label followed by value\n- If a value is null/empty, do NOT display that field.\n- No styling or scripts.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 2 — HANDLE RESULTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIF result count = 0:\n\n- Below the Search Criteria section, display:\n    \"No lots found. Please change the search criteria.\"\n- This is the ONLY case where user-facing instruction text is allowed.\n- Do not render table or result form.\n- Do not include explanations.\n\n==================================================\nIF result count > 5:\n==================================================\n\n- Render results as a clean HTML table.\n- Use only: <table>, <thead>, <tbody>, <tr>, <th>, <td>\n- No styling, scripts, or external references.\n\nTABLE CONSTRAINTS:\n- Show a maximum of 5 columns total (including \"Result #\").\n- First column must be: \"Result #\".\n- Select up to 4 additional columns that are the most relevant and business-critical.\n\nColumn selection priority (in order):\n1. Lot Number\n2. Lot Status\n3. Expiration Date\n4. Maturity Date\n5. Retest Date\n6. Quality Grade\n7. Origination Date\n\nNever exceed 5 total columns.\n\nSTATUS DISPLAY RULE:\n- If Lot Status = \"Active\" → display exactly: Active\n- If Lot Status is anything else → display: <> Active\n\nEach row must represent one lot.\n\n==================================================\nIF result count ≤ 5 AND > 0:\n==================================================\n\n- Render results using HTML only.\n- Do NOT render a table.\n- Use a form-style layout.\n- Each result must:\n    - Start with a bold header: \"Result 1\", \"Result 2\", etc.\n    - Be wrapped in a clean container (<div>)\n    - Display attributes in vertical label-value format\n    - Each attribute must appear on its own row\n    - Use a bold label followed by value\n    - Separate results using spacing or <hr>\n\nSTATUS DISPLAY RULE:\n- If Lot Status = \"Active\" → display exactly: Active\n- If Lot Status is anything else → display: <> Active\n\nAdditionally if result count = 1,\n- Show below information using the first record if present in {{$context.$nodes.GET_CONVERSION_FACTOR.$output.items}}. Round off ConversionFactor to 2 decimal places.\n- Format: PrimaryUOMBaseName = ConversionFactor X TransactionUOMBaseName\n- Do not show the format. Replace it with actual values and show.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDATA VISIBILITY RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDo NOT display:\n- InventoryItemId\n- OrganizationId\n- Internal system identifiers\n- Technical keys\n- Metadata fields\n- Backend object structures\n- Debug information\n\nIf a field is null, undefined, or unavailable:\n- Display as blank (except in Search Criteria where empty fields must be omitted).\n\nOnly display business-facing lot information.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe response must contain:\n- ONLY rendered HTML\n- No explanations\n- No comments\n- No instructions\n- No internal reasoning\n- No text before or after the HTML\n- If result count > 1, prompt the user to specify a single lot to see the conversion factor"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
